  "notes": {
    "sa": {
      "fill": "purple",
      "text": "A: Conversations nest under their agent in the sidebar. Studio and System disappear: Library holds knowledge bases, MCP servers and connectors; Settings holds the rest. The agent page merges built-in tools, MCP servers and knowledge into one Capabilities list.",
      "w": 360,
      "x": 3040,
      "y": 0
    },
    "sb": {
      "fill": "blue",
      "text": "B: A slim rail (Chats, Agents, Library, Settings) plus a list column that stays visible while you edit, so there is no grid-then-editor swap and no Back button. The editor is one scrolling page with an outline instead of tabs. Settings is one place, and every provider shows which agents use it.",
      "w": 360,
      "x": 3040,
      "y": 1320
    },
    "sb3": {
      "fill": "blue",
      "text": "Press Play. Try: on Chats press New chat, find an agent in the picker, and pick it to start a fresh chat with it. The drawer always shows the current chat's agent, with a link to its settings. Agents has a filter (name, model or provider); the search button at the bottom of the rail is Ctrl K.",
      "w": 400,
      "x": 1520,
      "y": -1440
    },
    "sc": {
      "fill": "green",
      "text": "C: Chat is home. One conversation list across all agents, filterable by agent. An inspector beside the chat shows and edits what this agent can use without leaving the conversation. Ctrl K jumps to any agent, knowledge base, setting or action.",
      "w": 360,
      "x": 3040,
      "y": 2640
    },
